  "curationSourceHash": "7066083909ece60946d719932bf06c10011418fb4f4d1ad883a2707185a9ffe8",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-21T22:05:43.985Z",
  "summary": "## Stripe Toolkit\n\nThe Stripe toolkit for Arcade connects LLM-powered agents to the Stripe API, enabling programmatic management of customers, products, pricing, invoicing, payments, and billing flows.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- **Customer management:** Create customers and list existing customer records.\n- **Product & pricing catalog:** Create and list products and prices (with automatic product creation when needed).\n- **Invoicing lifecycle:** Create invoices and invoice line items, finalize invoices, and list invoices.\n- **Payments & refunds:** List payment intents, issue refunds against a payment intent, and retrieve the current account balance.\n- **Payment links & billing portal:** Generate shareable payment links and create Stripe billing portal sessions for subscription self-service.\n\n## Secrets\n\n`STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` — A Stripe secret API key used to authenticate all requests to the Stripe API. To obtain one, log in to the [Stripe Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/), navigate to **Developers → API keys**, and copy the **Secret key** (prefixed `sk_live_` for production or `sk_test_` for test mode). Use a restricted key scoped to only the resources your agent needs (customers, invoices, products, prices, payment intents, refunds, balance, billing portal, and payment links) to follow least-privilege best practices. Never expose this key in client-side code.\n\nFor guidance on storing secrets in Arcade, see the [Arcade secrets docs](https://docs.arcade.dev/en/guides/create-tools/tool-basics/create-tool-secrets) and the [Arcade secrets dashboard](https://api.arcade.dev/dashboard/auth/secrets)."
